{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["And the reason for <b>And Abraham ran to the herd</b> is to declare the abundance of his zeal in generosity. For this great man who had in his household three hundred and eighteen trained swordsmen, and he himself was very old and weakened from his circumcision — he himself went to the tent of Sarah to hasten her in the making of the bread, and afterward ran to the place of the cattle to select from there a tender and good calf to prepare for his guests, and he did not do any of this through any one of the servants who stand before him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:14.543743616Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}